        <detaileddescription>
<para>Used by <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1compare__op" kindref="compound">compare_op</ref></computeroutput> for all six tags, so that a value within the tolerance is equal, and neither less nor greater; at least one operand must have an <computeroutput>epsilon</computeroutput> member (a floating-point literal, a <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated-literals_1ga5368740b47e92605914b6c38ea88aebf" kindref="member">to_f</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated-literals_1ga9608f4a6f0a61bc159a66a46fb8cd630" kindref="member">to_d</ref></computeroutput>, or <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated-literals_1gaeba32254fdd8159523b525745b13bfa9" kindref="member">to_ld</ref></computeroutput> wrapper, or <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated-literals_1gafe47800a219b00fcccf0a1dc596dbe20" kindref="member">approx()</ref></computeroutput>).</para>
<para>Used only by the deprecated floating-point wrappers, it is available only when <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-config_1ga67c701de5426ac340584ed038494a873" kindref="member">MICRO_OS_PLUS_MICRO_TEST_PLUS_DEPRECATED_ENABLED</ref></computeroutput> is defined.</para>
<para><xrefsect id="deprecated_1_deprecated000108"><xreftitle>Deprecated</xreftitle><xrefdescription><para>To be removed with the deprecated floating-point wrappers (since 6.0.0).</para>
