    <briefdescription>
<para>Definitions kept for compatibility with earlier releases. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The definitions in this group, and in the groups they refer to, are still available, but the compiler reports their use, and they will be removed in a future major release. Each one names its replacement in the deprecation message, together with the version that deprecated it (most of them since 6.0.0).</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Availability</title><para>The deprecated definitions are compiled only when the application defines the macro <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-config_1ga67c701de5426ac340584ed038494a873" kindref="member">MICRO_OS_PLUS_MICRO_TEST_PLUS_DEPRECATED_ENABLED</ref></computeroutput>, in <computeroutput>micro-os-plus/project-config.h</computeroutput> or in <computeroutput>micro-os-plus/micro-test-plus-defines.h</computeroutput>. Without it, the applications that still use them fail to compile, which is a way of finding what must be migrated.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="par"><title>Groups</title><para>The deprecated definitions are documented together with the features they belong to:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>the overloaded comparison and logical operators, in <ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated-operators" kindref="compound">Operators</ref>, replaced by the function comparators and the logical functions;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>the user-defined literals and the type wrappers, in <ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated-literals" kindref="compound">Literals and Wrappers</ref>, replaced by the plain values passed to the function comparators;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>the underscore-prefixed logical functions (<computeroutput>_not()</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>_and()</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>_or()</computeroutput>), in <ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated-logical-functions" kindref="compound">Logical Functions</ref>, replaced by <computeroutput>negate()</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>all_of()</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>any_of()</computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="par"><title>Other deprecated definitions</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>the v5.0.1 names of the classes: <computeroutput>static_runner</computeroutput> (replaced by <computeroutput>runner</computeroutput>), <computeroutput>subtest</computeroutput> (replaced by <computeroutput>test_case</computeroutput>), <computeroutput>detail::runner_totals</computeroutput> (replaced by <computeroutput>counters</computeroutput>), and <computeroutput>detail::timestamps</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>detail::timestamp</computeroutput>, which are internal and not replaced;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>runner (const char*)</computeroutput>, replaced by <computeroutput>runner()</computeroutput> followed by <computeroutput>add_top_suite()</computeroutput> (since 4.1.0);</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>runner::initialise (argc, argv, top_suite_name)</computeroutput>, replaced by <computeroutput>initialise (argc, argv)</computeroutput> followed by <computeroutput>add_top_suite()</computeroutput>;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>runner::exit_code()</computeroutput>, replaced by <computeroutput>runner::run_suites()</computeroutput>;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>runner::suite()</computeroutput>, replaced by <computeroutput>runner::add_suite()</computeroutput>;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>runner::suites_count()</computeroutput>, replaced by <computeroutput>added_suites_count()</computeroutput> or <computeroutput>total_suites_count()</computeroutput>;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>runner::verbosity()</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>runner::reporter()</computeroutput> with its <computeroutput>verbosity()</computeroutput> member, replaced by <computeroutput>runner::verbosity_level()</computeroutput>;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>runner::timings()</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>test_case::timings()</computeroutput>, and the members of <computeroutput>detail::stopwatch</computeroutput> kept from the v5.0.1 timestamps, which are internal and not replaced;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>the <computeroutput>counters</computeroutput> members <computeroutput>successful_checks()</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>executed_subtests()</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>was_successful()</computeroutput>, replaced by <computeroutput>passed_checks()</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>executed_test_cases()</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>passed()</computeroutput> (the deprecated mutators <computeroutput>increment_successful_checks()</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>increment_executed_subtests()</computeroutput> were removed, since the counters are updated only by the framework);</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>test_case::assume()</computeroutput>, replaced by <computeroutput>test_case::require()</computeroutput>;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>the overloads of <computeroutput>test_case::expect()</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>test_case::require()</computeroutput> that accept an argument that is always true (a string literal or a function name), replaced by writing the condition;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>the <computeroutput>static_suite</computeroutput> constructor whose callable takes a <computeroutput>static_suite&amp;</computeroutput>, replaced by a callable taking a <computeroutput>suite&amp;</computeroutput>;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>reflection::short_name()</computeroutput>, replaced by <computeroutput>utility::extract_file_name()</computeroutput>;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>the <computeroutput>type_traits</computeroutput> namespace, with the concepts and the value wrapper templates of v5.0.1, replaced by the <computeroutput>extension</computeroutput> namespace.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="par"><title>Migration</title><para>Build once with the deprecation warnings enabled, and rewrite each reported use as suggested by the message. Temporarily, the warnings can be disabled with <computeroutput>-Wno-deprecated-declarations</computeroutput>, for the applications that build with <computeroutput>-Werror</computeroutput>.</para>
</simplesect>
